.TH ___CHTTPCLIENT_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-14" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
___chttpclient_destroy \- RAII cleanup function for chttpcli
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

___chttpclient_destroy(chttpcli *pp);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Static inline function used as the cleanup callback in
chttpcli_declare_scoped() and chttpcli_construct_scoped(). If *pp is
not CHTTPCLI_INVALID, calls __chttpclient_destroy(*pp) and sets *pp
to CHTTPCLI_INVALID.

This function is not intended to be called directly; use
chttpcli_declare_scoped() or chttpcli_construct_scoped() instead.

Calling __chttpclient_destroy on a stale (already destroyed) handle
is a FATAL ERROR (abort()/SIGABRT); see __chttpclient_destroy(3).
This is only reachable here if *pp was left holding a stale value
by code outside the normal declare/construct-scoped lifecycle, since
the scoped macros themselves always leave *pp either live or already
CHTTPCLI_INVALID.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
pp  Pointer to a chttpcli variable (must not be NULL).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Compatible with __attribute__((cleanup)) on GCC and Clang.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpcli_declare_scoped (3),
.BR chttpcli_construct_scoped (3),
.BR __chttpclient_destroy (3),
.BR chttpclient_destroy (3)
